id: pm-slack-standup-toolchain-1104
title: Adopt the 2026.11.4 toolchain and literal SDK field contract
description: "Supersede Dependabot PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack-standup/pull/186 with a reviewed toolchain migration. Verify seeded SDK fixtures against literal typed fields and preserve all native-state assertions."
type: Chore
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[4]: dependencies,"gh:unbraind/pm-slack-standup#186",migration,sdk
created_at: "2026-11-05T04:49:24.949Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-05T05:54:18.381Z"
author: codex-toolchain-1104
acceptance_criteria: Exact requested pins; focused regressions and coverage pass; typecheck and lint pass; separate review PR contains tracker evidence
comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-05T04:50:11.015Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Cause (test): pm-cli 2026.10.30 GH-1614 keeps typed SDK fields literal. The shared progressScope passes parent/sprint/release/assignee none on create and update; commitment-variance reproduces placeholder refusal before its assertions. Replace fixture scalars with unset lists, retaining all seeded model and race assertions. GH-1577 already makes create focus inheritance opt-in; explicit unsets keep the fixture contract on both creates and updates. No production sentinel use found."
  "2026-11-05T05:20:15.103Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Focused commitment-variance file passes 10/10 after explicit SDK unsets; typecheck, lint, build, test compilation, strict tracker health and changelog regeneration/check pass. Fresh tracked dist and changelog outputs are unchanged. The complete coverage gate runs through pm test with original 500-sequence assertions and all four thresholds at 100. Author normalization on the unpublished review branch preserves the inherited commit tree and leaves the original Dependabot ref intact."
  "2026-11-05T05:42:47.774Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Complete npm coverage attempt: 358 tests, 356 passed, two failed, zero skipped/canceled. Both 500-sequence native/SDK models complete with zero mismatches, including all 2000 progress mutations. Remaining cause (test/runtime): both real packed matrices in test/accept-packed.test.ts reach the unchanged 290000 ms outer subprocess deadline (null exit status); stderr advances through npm-current/bun-current. This is the previously tracked packed timing class, not a proven new SDK semantic regression. Diagnostic aggregate coverage is lines/statements 96.21, branches 99.88, functions 97.63 percent; accept-packed.ts is only partially exercised and the failed gate removes its public receipt. Keep all thresholds, scenarios and deadlines. Rerun the failing file alone before final handoff."
  "2026-11-05T05:54:14.587Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Isolated packed file rerun completed 15 tests: 13 passed, two failed, zero skipped/canceled. Both failures again hit the unchanged 290000 ms outer subprocess deadline (about 292 seconds observed), so the local timing blocker reproduces outside the full-suite model workload. No deadline, source inventory, scenario, count or coverage threshold was changed. Publish the verified GH-1614 fixture migration with complete 356/358 full-suite evidence and failed diagnostic coverage; full green gates remain for exact-head CI and orchestrator verification. No new upstream semantic regression is established."
